        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Graph and Manifold Embedding\n",
        "\n",
        "PCA is a linear embedding method. K-means and hierarchical clustering are direct clustering methods. This chapter discusses methods that use neighborhood or graph structure to represent data in a lower-dimensional space.\n",
        "\n",
        "The main methods are:\n",
        "\n",
        "- spectral clustering,\n",
        "- self-organizing maps,\n",
        "- UMAP.\n",
        "\n",
        "These methods are useful when the structure is nonlinear or when ordinary Euclidean clusters are not adequate.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Spectral Clustering\n",
        "\n",
        "Spectral clustering is useful when clusters are not well separated by simple Euclidean centroids. It uses a graph representation of the data.\n",
        "\n",
        "The main steps are:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Build an adjacency matrix $W$ that measures similarity between observations.\n",
        "2. Construct a graph Laplacian from $W$.\n",
        "3. Use eigenvectors of the Laplacian to embed the data into a lower-dimensional space.\n",
        "4. Run k-means on the embedded features.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-note}\n",
        "## Main idea\n",
        "\n",
        "Spectral clustering turns a clustering problem into a graph partitioning problem.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "### Adjacency Matrix\n",
        "\n",
        "One common similarity is the Gaussian similarity:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "W_{ij}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\exp\\left(\n",
        "-\\frac{\\|x_i-x_j\\|^2}{2\\sigma^2}\n",
        "\\right).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Another option is a nearest-neighbor graph, where two observations are connected if one is among the other's nearest neighbors.\n",
        "\n",
        "The adjacency matrix describes which observations are close in the graph.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Graph Laplacian\n",
        "\n",
        "Let $D$ be the diagonal degree matrix:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "D_{ii}=\\sum_j W_{ij}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The unnormalized graph Laplacian is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "L=D-W.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "A normalized version is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "L_{\\text{sym}}\n",
        "=\n",
        "I-D^{-1/2}WD^{-1/2}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Eigenvectors of these matrices give an embedding that reflects graph connectivity.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Concentric Circles Example\n",
        "\n",
        "K-means struggles with concentric circles because the clusters are not separated by centers."
      ],
      "id": "3c2b924e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
