        "Spectral clustering can recover clusters based on connectivity rather than center separation.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-caution}\n",
        "## Spectral clustering tuning\n",
        "\n",
        "The graph construction matters. Results can change with `n_neighbors`, kernel bandwidth, or affinity type.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Self-Organizing Maps\n",
        "\n",
        "A self-organizing map (SOM) is an unsupervised neural network method for representing high-dimensional data on a low-dimensional grid.\n",
        "\n",
        "The usual SOM grid is two-dimensional. Each grid cell has a prototype vector. During training:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Pick an observation.\n",
        "2. Find the closest prototype, called the best matching unit.\n",
        "3. Move that prototype and its grid neighbors toward the observation.\n",
        "4. Repeat many times.\n",
        "\n",
        "The result is a grid where nearby cells tend to represent similar observations.\n",
        "\n",
        "SOMs are often used for:\n",
        "\n",
        "- visualization,\n",
        "- exploratory clustering,\n",
        "- topology-preserving maps,\n",
        "- summarizing high-dimensional observations.\n",
        "\n",
        "Python does not include SOM in `sklearn`. A common lightweight package is `MiniSom`. Install it only if needed:\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.bash}\n",
        "uv add minisom\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Example code:"
      ],
      "id": "c8f2af49"
    },
