        "::: {.callout-note}\n",
        "## SOM interpretation\n",
        "\n",
        "SOM is mainly exploratory. The grid is useful for visualization, but the result depends on grid size, learning rate, neighborhood width, and training length.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## UMAP\n",
        "\n",
        "UMAP stands for Uniform Manifold Approximation and Projection. It is a nonlinear dimension reduction method often used for visualization.\n",
        "\n",
        "UMAP is graph-based. It builds a local-neighborhood graph in the original space and then finds a low-dimensional embedding that preserves much of that neighborhood structure.\n",
        "\n",
        "It is related in spirit to spectral embedding and t-SNE:\n",
        "\n",
        "- PCA is linear and variance-based.\n",
        "- Spectral embedding is graph/eigenvector-based.\n",
        "- t-SNE and UMAP are nonlinear graph-based visualization methods.\n",
        "\n",
        "UMAP is not part of core `sklearn`. The common package is `umap-learn`.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.bash}\n",
        "uv add umap-learn\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Example:"
      ],
      "id": "a68e3df8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| eval: false\n",
        "import umap\n",
        "from sklearn.datasets import load_iris\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
        "\n",
        "iris = load_iris(as_frame=True)\n",
        "X_iris = iris.data\n",
        "y_iris = iris.target\n",
        "\n",
        "X_scaled = StandardScaler().fit_transform(X_iris)\n",
        "\n",
        "reducer = umap.UMAP(\n",
        "    n_neighbors=15,\n",
        "    min_dist=0.1,\n",
        "    n_components=2,\n",
        "    random_state=1,\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "X_umap = reducer.fit_transform(X_scaled)\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(6, 5))\n",
        "plt.scatter(X_umap[:, 0], X_umap[:, 1], c=y_iris, edgecolor=\"k\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"UMAP1\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"UMAP2\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Iris UMAP\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
