      "source": [
        "### UMAP Tuning\n",
        "\n",
        "Important tuning parameters include:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Parameter | Meaning |\n",
        "|---|---|\n",
        "| `n_neighbors` | Size of local neighborhood used to build the graph. |\n",
        "| `min_dist` | How tightly points can be packed in the embedding. |\n",
        "| `n_components` | Dimension of the embedding. Usually 2 or 3 for visualization. |\n",
        "| `metric` | Distance metric in the original space. |\n",
        "\n",
        "Small `n_neighbors` emphasizes local structure. Large `n_neighbors` emphasizes more global structure.\n",
        "\n",
        "Small `min_dist` allows tighter clusters in the embedding. Larger `min_dist` spreads points out.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-caution}\n",
        "## UMAP plots\n",
        "\n",
        "UMAP is a visualization method, not proof of true clusters. Apparent gaps in a UMAP plot can be affected by tuning choices.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Comparing Methods\n",
        "\n",
        "| Method | Main purpose | Strength | Limitation |\n",
        "|---|---|---|---|\n",
        "| PCA | Linear dimension reduction | Interpretable directions and variance explained | Only linear structure |\n",
        "| Spectral clustering | Graph-based clustering | Handles non-convex clusters | Graph tuning matters |\n",
        "| SOM | Grid-based exploratory map | Topology-preserving visualization | Extra package and tuning |\n",
        "| UMAP | Nonlinear visualization | Strong visual embeddings | Tuning-sensitive and not a formal clustering model |\n",
        "\n",
        "## Summary\n",
        "\n",
        "Spectral clustering:\n",
        "\n",
        "- clusters using graph connectivity,\n",
        "- can handle non-convex clusters,\n",
        "- depends strongly on graph construction.\n",
        "\n",
        "SOM:\n",
        "\n",
        "- maps high-dimensional observations to a low-dimensional grid,\n",
        "- is mainly exploratory,\n",
        "- depends on grid and training parameters.\n",
        "\n",
        "UMAP:\n",
        "\n",
        "- creates nonlinear low-dimensional embeddings,\n",
        "- is useful for visualization,\n",
        "- depends strongly on tuning choices.\n",
        "\n",
        "Graph and manifold methods can reveal structure that linear methods and ordinary clustering may miss, but the resulting plots should be interpreted carefully."
      ],
